GNU GRUB 2.12 BIOS installer tools
=================================

Slax stores the BIOS installation payload at slax/boot/grub/bios/tools.tar.xz.
Both native installers read it from the selected Slax source, including an ISO,
Slax directory or complete copy-to-RAM source. The Windows installer does not
embed these files, and the Linux installer does not require installed GRUB tools.

The archive contains matching i386-pc modules and separate Windows and Linux
versions of grub-mkimage and grub-fstest. The image utility creates an LZMA-compressed
BIOS core for the approved disk and partition. The filesystem verifier checks
actual access and compares copied boot files before BIOS activation. Matching
runtime modules are then copied into the installed Slax boot directory.

installer/build-grub compiles the unmodified GNU helpers during the Slax installer
build. Linux helpers use shared system libc and liblzma5, built in the same
glibc 2.27 sysroot as the Linux installer. Windows helpers target
Windows XP onward and use only system DLLs, with static, threadless liblzma.
No compiler, GRUB package, external unpacker or installation-time network is needed.

The shared i386-pc files come from the verified official GNU Windows release:
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/grub/grub-2.12-for-windows.zip
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/grub/grub-2.12-for-windows.zip.sig
