XZ 5.8.1 source for Windows (Debian mirror of the upstream archive):
https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/x/xz-utils/xz-utils_5.8.1.orig.tar.xz
SHA256: 0b54f79df85912504de0b14aec7971e3f964491af1812d83447005807513cd9e
https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz/releases/tag/v5.8.1
liblzma uses the Zero-Clause BSD license (0BSD):
https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz/blob/v5.8.1/COPYING
The Windows installer also links its static decoder to unpack the trusted BIOS
payload. The Linux installer uses shared system liblzma5; Linux builds require
liblzma-dev instead of a private XZ build.

The deterministic USTAR archive contains only regular files, compressed with XZ
and CRC64. Its SHA256 and exact compressed/uncompressed sizes are compiled into
both installers. Helpers are executed only after the selected source's archive
matches that trusted build. The archive and both prebuilt installers must be
rebuilt and distributed together. Ordinary ISO builds copy that matching set.
Downloaded source archives and extracted upstream build inputs stay outside Git.

This payload is only for legacy BIOS installation. Debian's signed shim, signed
UEFI GRUB and signed kernel remain separate under slax/boot/EFI/BOOT and retain
Secure Boot verification. These helper builds do not modify those signed files.
